<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Eliot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1819">1819</a>–<a href="/years/1880">1880</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mary Ann Evans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Eliot was the pen name of Mary Ann Evans, an English novelist and one of the leading writers of the Victorian era. Her novels, including Adam <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a>, The Mill on the Floss, Silas Marner and Middlemarch, are known for their psychological depth and realistic portrayal of provincial English life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-eliot.jpg" alt="George Eliot" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: replica by François D’Albert Durade (1804–1886) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Eliot,_por_Fran%C3%A7ois_D%27Albert_Durade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
